+# CI triage: build 1192
+
+- Root cause: the zero-padding change rewrote `parse_price` (src/shopcore/csv_import.py) to parse via `float()` and return `Decimal(round(number, places))`, i.e. a Decimal built from a binary float.
+- Most cent values (19.99, 999.99, 4.35) have no exact binary representation, so prices came back as 19.98999999999999843... and the exact-price assertions in the CSV tests failed; very large prices were also silently altered.
+- Fix: parse and validate with `Decimal` only, `quantize` to the currency's minor unit, and reject the value if quantizing changes it, so zero padding is still accepted and returned with the currency's decimal places.
+- Added a regression test that parsed cent prices are exact decimals.
